# Production-only env layer (loaded when APP_ENV=production). Committed on
# purpose: it holds 1Password *references*, not secret values. Varlock
# resolves every reference in the loaded graph and treats failure as fatal,
# so ONLY references a production build actually consumes belong here — a
# ref without a real-env override breaks Cloudflare Pages builds, which have
# no 1Password CLI. Real env vars with the same name take precedence, which
# is how the Pages-configured SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN wins over this reference
# (and how local manual builds fall back to the 1Password desktop app).
#
# The Cloudflare vars (CF_ACCOUNT_ID, CLOUDFLARE_AI_TOKEN) deliberately do
# NOT appear here yet: nothing consumes them until Phase 3, and their op()
# refs made Pages production builds fail. Phase 3 must reintroduce them
# with real-env values configured on Pages (see the deployment runbook).
SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=op(op://dev/araowl-sentry/auth-token)
